Add runtime absolute-touch bounds control over Moonlight local-control.

This extends the absolute-touch patch from static launch-time bounds to a
runtime input command. The input command is Moonlight-local: it mutates the
client evdev filter before input packets are sent, and it is intentionally
separate from Sunshine runtime-setting commands.

Managed dynamic mode can pass -absolutetouchrequirebounds so absolute-touch
input fails closed until either startup fallback bounds or runtime bounds are
active. Bounds are stored as one coherent evdev snapshot guarded by a mutex, so
local-control updates do not race the evdev reader through independent globals.

